o(6,3,'text','About 44 minutes')
o(6,3,'explanation','1 GiB / 32 KiB = 32,768 exchanges; at 0.08 seconds each that is 2,621.44 seconds, or 43.69 minutes.')
u(6,['workedExample'],'There are 2^30 / 2^15 = 32,768 blocks. At 0.080 s per block the time is 2,621.44 s, about 43.69 minutes. Throughput is 400 KiB/s, or 3.2768 Mbit/s.\n\nAn idealised batch of 64 outstanding reads transfers 2 MiB per RTT and takes 40.96 seconds for the same file. Real transfer time also depends on bandwidth, channel windows, processing and partial responses. OpenSSH documents a default maximum of 64 concurrent requests; that does not guarantee this ideal throughput.')
u(7,['prompt'],'Assuming sound key exchange and signature algorithms, SSH public-key authentication signs data including the session ID. Which signature-reuse attacks does this resist? Select all that apply.')
