o(11,1,'text','If the client deadline expires before completion, the call reports DEADLINE_EXCEEDED and cancellation can signal servers to stop; applications must cooperate')
o(11,1,'explanation','Cancellation is not an instantaneous distributed stop. Transport delays and application behaviour matter, and effects already committed are not rolled back.')
u(11,['workedExample'],'A starts with 300 ms and has used 50 ms, leaving about 250 ms. It can give B that remaining budget, or reserve time for its own response. Deadline propagation support depends on the library and application configuration. A client deadline can cancel an HTTP/2 stream; server handlers should check cancellation and stop unnecessary work. Timers do not fire everywhere simultaneously, and cancellation cannot undo an already committed side effect. Units: H hours, M minutes, S seconds, m milliseconds, u microseconds, n nanoseconds.')
